      ],
      "message": "mempool: clamp future mempool.dat entry times\n\nA mempool.dat entry with a time in the future is loaded as it is, so its\ntransaction never expires, whatever -mempoolexpiry says.\n\nI use the current time for such an entry. Earlier times are unchanged.\nOpen PR #36540 removes time-based expiry, which would make this change\nmoot. I tested this with a functional test that restarts a node with its\nclock behind a saved entry time. It fails without the change and passes\nwith it.",
